WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.480
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.750 --> 00:03.100
Where the hell is Shiharu?

3
00:03.100 --> 00:05.980
Let's talk in person. Alone.

4
00:05.980 --> 00:10.400
Please help me find Shiharu Nanase.

5
00:10.400 --> 00:12.150
So, what's your next move?

6
00:12.150 --> 00:14.020
The same as it's always been.

7
00:14.020 --> 00:16.410
Find my sister.

8
00:21.150 --> 00:22.830
[Keita]

9
00:28.480 --> 00:32.350
[log.8]

10
00:32.350 --> 00:35.420
Bones again?

11
00:35.420 --> 00:36.950
Yes.

12
00:42.400 --> 00:44.980
Well, we can't do much else here.

13
00:44.980 --> 00:47.940
I'll escort Kayoko Senba to the hospital.

14
00:47.940 --> 00:49.290
Alright.

15
00:58.400 --> 01:00.450
Where'd you get the battle scars?

16
01:03.270 --> 01:05.250
Plantae?

17
01:05.250 --> 01:07.150
I don't know.

18
01:07.150 --> 01:09.730
It may have been Xin Ming Ah.

19
01:09.730 --> 01:12.020
Xin Ming Ah?

20
01:12.020 --> 01:14.810
The conglomerate trying to buy out Nichie?

21
01:14.810 --> 01:16.770
Why'd they attack you?

22
01:16.770 --> 01:18.800
Beats me.

23
01:18.800 --> 01:22.870
If you want my information, you'd better start spilling.

24
01:22.870 --> 01:26.120
I really don't know.

25
01:27.270 --> 01:31.850
Then do you know where Haruka Nanase is?

26
01:31.850 --> 01:34.560
He's gone and disappeared again.

27
01:34.560 --> 01:38.460
I bet he's somehow tied to this case, too.

28
01:40.710 --> 01:44.770
I expect something juicy in exchange.

29
01:44.770 --> 01:47.220
Fine, just tell me where he is!

30
01:49.790 --> 01:52.510
This case has taken enough victims already.

31
01:54.130 --> 01:56.120
A bit late to the game, eh?

32
01:56.690 --> 01:59.300
It's about damn time you took this seriously.

33
02:07.320 --> 02:12.850
Is the man named Ushio involved in this case as well?

34
02:15.150 --> 02:21.150
Professor Ishimizaki's daughter was seen on your intercom.

35
02:21.150 --> 02:24.300
What is your relationship to her?

36
02:26.690 --> 02:32.220
I first met her at Ishimizaki's funeral.

37
02:34.330 --> 02:37.000
We've met several times since.

38
02:38.280 --> 02:43.160
We would trade stories about him.

39
02:43.940 --> 02:47.740
The same substance was used to kill Professor Ishimizaki,

40
02:47.740 --> 02:53.430
and to make an attempt on Haruka Nanase's life.

41
02:54.460 --> 02:56.800
It was most likely used here as well.

42
02:58.440 --> 03:02.960
These cases are likely tied to one another.

43
03:07.150 --> 03:10.010
Please, just leave me alone.

44
03:13.070 --> 03:16.260
You know of Shiharu Nanase, yes?

45
03:20.130 --> 03:22.730
Please, tell us where she is.

46
03:22.730 --> 03:24.680
I don't know.

47
03:26.060 --> 03:29.080
I know nothing!

48
03:40.690 --> 03:42.680
Why is there an officer here?

49
03:43.690 --> 03:46.340
Tomoe Senba was killed.

50
03:48.400 --> 03:53.450
Her bones and her son Keita's shoes

51
03:53.450 --> 03:56.550
were delivered to Kayoko Senba's room earlier this morning.

52
03:57.990 --> 03:59.820
No...

53
03:59.820 --> 04:03.640
She was probably killed long before today.

54
04:04.670 --> 04:07.450
- This is my fault. - No.

55
04:07.450 --> 04:10.430
It's the work of that organization Senba is involved with.

56
04:11.240 --> 04:14.580
She's to blame for associating with them as well.

57
04:14.580 --> 04:16.690
Besides, the actual culprit is Ushio.

58
04:16.690 --> 04:19.240
- But... - It's not your fault.

59
04:20.310 --> 04:24.620
Hirama filled me in.

60
04:25.210 --> 04:28.220
Honestly, I can't believe it.

61
04:28.820 --> 04:33.200
Nichie created a human clone, right?

62
04:34.280 --> 04:38.330
That's so ridiculous, I'm still not entirely convinced.

63
04:38.330 --> 04:40.680
Could you tell me more about it?

64
04:41.910 --> 04:45.650
Tada wants to trade information with us.

65
04:45.650 --> 04:50.340
Tell him what we know, and he'll share his intel.

66
04:51.300 --> 04:52.880
Including anything about your sister.

67
04:52.880 --> 04:56.830
Yeah. If we find a lead, you'll be the first to know.

68
04:59.290 --> 05:03.010
You don't want more people dying, do you?

69
05:06.610 --> 05:07.920
No, I don't.

70
05:09.580 --> 05:12.050
What do you wish to know?

71
05:12.050 --> 05:17.680
Your sister was created to be Plantae's founder, right?

72
05:17.680 --> 05:22.950
Right. She's still alive. That's why the deaths haven't stopped.

73
05:22.950 --> 05:24.980
Exactly.

74
05:25.770 --> 05:31.300
We think your sister ordered a strike on Tomoe.

75
05:32.820 --> 05:34.820
That accusation again?

76
05:34.820 --> 05:38.640
Your sister is the Holy Woman.

77
05:38.640 --> 05:43.580
Yeah. It's clear she could give the order.

78
05:45.210 --> 05:50.200
That's the first conclusion I reached hearing Hirama's account.

79
05:50.950 --> 05:55.850
If your sister's alive, she's the mastermind.

80
05:55.850 --> 05:59.520
You're saying Shiharu had both Tomoe and Professor Ishimizaki killed?

81
05:59.520 --> 06:02.000
If we don't hurry, Keita's next.

82
06:02.000 --> 06:04.350
She would never.

83
06:04.350 --> 06:08.410
Your sister's the leader of Plantae!

84
06:08.410 --> 06:09.800
- Say what? - Calm down.

85
06:09.800 --> 06:12.180
Shiharu wouldn't murder a child!

86
06:12.180 --> 06:15.750
We're trying to keep you safe!

87
06:34.750 --> 06:37.620
Please wait here. The President will see you shortly.

88
06:38.770 --> 06:42.660
You seem quite busy these days, Maehara.

89
06:42.660 --> 06:46.790
How are your frequent trips to Nichie City?

90
06:48.400 --> 06:51.220
I am always busy.

91
06:51.920 --> 06:54.750
And underlings are made to run errands.

92
06:55.620 --> 06:57.620
I expect you would understand.

93
07:00.080 --> 07:04.510
I can quit at any time, and find employment elsewhere.

94
07:05.310 --> 07:08.790
I pity those who do not have such leisure.

95
07:08.790 --> 07:14.770
Like underlings who obey their superiors, only to be tossed away on a whim.

96
07:20.060 --> 07:21.930
I appreciate your patience.

97
07:24.020 --> 07:27.770
What can I do for you today?

98
07:27.770 --> 07:32.620
I wish to ask about the bills that he has been covering up.

99
07:35.980 --> 07:40.810
Maehara is re-evaluating the fees you specifically requested we look into.

100
07:40.810 --> 07:42.410
It seems there has been a misunderstanding.

101
07:42.410 --> 07:45.100
Is that so.

102
07:45.100 --> 07:50.000
Then I am allowed to speak the truth in his presence?

103
07:50.530 --> 07:52.290
The truth?

104
07:52.980 --> 07:55.230
- What... - Though I'd love to talk more,

105
07:55.230 --> 07:58.020
I'm unfortunately short on time today.

106
07:58.020 --> 08:00.660
I will reach out, so let us speak some other time.

107
08:01.530 --> 08:03.200
Understood.

108
08:07.520 --> 08:10.790
I can see myself out, thank you very much.

109
08:22.100 --> 08:23.810
I will handle this case myself.

110
08:23.810 --> 08:29.510
Sir, what is your ultimate goal with Nichie Pharmaceutical?

111
08:33.160 --> 08:36.410
I would do anything for the company.

112
08:37.240 --> 08:39.310
I want you to trust me.

113
08:39.310 --> 08:41.590
What is going on behind the scenes?

114
08:42.820 --> 08:47.710
I have no "ultimate goal" for this company.

115
08:49.350 --> 08:55.620
I have my hands full cleaning up the mess the founder left me.

116
08:57.850 --> 09:02.690
That man will come to you with a deal.

117
09:02.690 --> 09:06.730
If you do not accept, he will go public with his information.

118
09:06.730 --> 09:08.900
- And... - Maehara.

119
09:08.900 --> 09:11.630
I said I would handle this case.

120
09:13.810 --> 09:15.840
I met with Haruka.

121
09:18.620 --> 09:22.050
He said he had data pertaining to Roopkund.

122
09:24.300 --> 09:27.540
He asked me where Shiharu was.

123
09:29.660 --> 09:32.620
Can't you tell me the truth?

124
09:39.150 --> 09:41.040
What is it you want to do?

125
09:43.100 --> 09:48.180
I will obey your every order, sir.

126
09:49.910 --> 09:53.060
I will stick to my convictions.

127
09:53.060 --> 09:55.960
You will stick to yours.

128
10:01.440 --> 10:08.550
Even if our goals differ?

129
10:10.710 --> 10:12.290
That's right.

130
10:18.050 --> 10:25.890
[Is his step-sister the mastermind?] [The truth shrouded in mystery and betrayal]

131
10:37.180 --> 10:42.010
Excuse me, an individual claiming to be Senba's relative has come to visit.

132
10:42.510 --> 10:43.870
Let them through.

133
10:50.520 --> 10:52.220
Nanase!

134
10:57.350 --> 10:59.410
I'm sorry about earlier.

135
11:00.560 --> 11:02.830
I should've been more considerate.

136
11:03.650 --> 11:07.250
But I want to solve this. You have to understand.

137
11:09.150 --> 11:14.270
Can you tell me more about this cloning tech?

138
11:14.270 --> 11:17.480
You have evidence to prove it exists, right?

139
11:17.480 --> 11:19.750
Otherwise you wouldn't be so certain.

140
11:20.480 --> 11:23.020
If you have something, they'll come after you.

141
11:23.020 --> 11:25.100
I don't want anyone else to die.

142
11:25.100 --> 11:26.520
Could you entrust it with us?

143
11:26.520 --> 11:28.850
I already destroyed it.

144
11:28.850 --> 11:30.130
What?

145
11:30.130 --> 11:32.700
There never was any evidence.

146
11:32.700 --> 11:35.250
Quit messing around, a child is in danger!

147
11:35.250 --> 11:37.950
You said I had no sister.

148
11:38.830 --> 11:41.960
Why would I have evidence of a person who never existed?

149
11:42.530 --> 11:46.040
- You... - I never lied to you people, not once!

150
11:48.290 --> 11:51.850
Would this have happened if you had actually listened?

151
11:51.850 --> 11:53.530
But no one believed me.

152
11:53.530 --> 11:54.980
That's not true.

153
11:54.980 --> 11:56.780
We looked into what you said.

154
11:56.780 --> 11:59.330
And that didn't stop the deaths, did it?

155
12:00.060 --> 12:04.480
If they weren't going to believe in the first place, evidence won't help.

156
12:04.480 --> 12:07.080
- That's not true. - But it is.

157
12:07.080 --> 12:08.700
Besides...

158
12:09.850 --> 12:12.240
You people can't stop this now.

159
12:24.270 --> 12:27.040
Dr. Senba, it's Kasuga. I'm coming in.

160
12:29.460 --> 12:32.170
Goodness, you look terrible.

161
12:33.730 --> 12:36.160
I want to help you.

162
12:40.710 --> 12:44.990
If you're scared to return home, come with us.

163
12:44.990 --> 12:48.460
We're all worried about you, Dr. Senba.

164
12:50.850 --> 12:54.230
So long as we remain in touch, you may leave.

165
12:54.230 --> 12:56.940
I will come to ask questions another day.

166
12:56.940 --> 12:59.670
- But... - You do not need to worry.

167
12:59.670 --> 13:02.340
Just come with me.

168
13:04.430 --> 13:08.790
- Yes? - That way, everyone will be safe.

169
13:29.420 --> 13:32.220
What is going on here?

170
13:33.780 --> 13:35.740
Will you people kill me next?

171
13:35.740 --> 13:38.520
You do not need to worry.

172
13:38.520 --> 13:41.250
We are doing this to protect you.

173
13:49.810 --> 13:53.220
Please, tell me what happened.

174
13:55.280 --> 13:59.050
I need you to tell me the truth.

175
14:01.060 --> 14:05.150
I know you met Haruka Nanase at Ishimizaki's grave.

176
14:05.150 --> 14:08.270
I had been tailing you both.

177
14:08.270 --> 14:11.120
What did you tell him? Out with it!

178
14:16.020 --> 14:21.310
I have a duty to protect my family.

179
14:21.310 --> 14:26.200
So please, tell me what happened.

180
14:31.310 --> 14:33.500
Keita...

181
14:36.020 --> 14:37.620
Where is Keita?

182
14:49.850 --> 14:53.040
Haruka? Did you figure something out?

183
14:53.690 --> 14:56.350
You shouldn't associate with me any more.

184
14:56.350 --> 14:58.200
What? Why?

185
14:59.060 --> 15:02.720
I met Mayuzumi yesterday.

186
15:04.020 --> 15:07.520
We were actually supposed to see each other today as well.

187
15:07.520 --> 15:09.600
The investigator?

188
15:09.600 --> 15:13.000
She said she wants to search for Shiharu.

189
15:13.540 --> 15:14.790
What?

190
15:15.530 --> 15:18.440
She told me Shiharu doesn't exist.

191
15:18.440 --> 15:24.020
That's because she doesn't appear on any family register.

192
15:24.020 --> 15:26.500
But apparently that's a thing that can happen.

193
15:27.230 --> 15:29.100
So?

194
15:29.100 --> 15:37.320
Mayuzumi says we can get her documented as someone without a registry.

195
15:37.320 --> 15:42.900
I thought it wouldn't be a bad idea to get her involved in the search.

196
15:42.900 --> 15:45.000
She'd be able to protect me, too.

197
15:47.810 --> 15:50.790
I think you're better off lying low for now.

198
15:51.520 --> 15:54.160
Any one of us could be killed off next.

199
15:57.200 --> 16:01.410
I can't stand not being able to do anything.

200
16:02.150 --> 16:05.400
Everyone's only focused on their own selfish goals.

201
16:05.400 --> 16:10.290
No one actually cares about whether you, or Shiharu are safe.

202
16:13.310 --> 16:15.310
Are you outside right now?

203
16:15.310 --> 16:16.910
Yeah.

204
16:16.910 --> 16:18.980
You should get home immediately.

205
16:18.980 --> 16:21.500
You never know who's watching.

206
16:24.480 --> 16:26.170
Okay.

207
16:45.730 --> 16:48.100
You really came alone.

208
16:48.100 --> 16:52.250
Of course. I am on your side.

209
16:55.270 --> 16:59.390
How much do you know?

210
17:00.070 --> 17:03.790
I am aware you created a human clone.

211
17:04.650 --> 17:09.380
One from a corpse at that.

212
17:10.940 --> 17:13.310
And if I said I know nothing of it?

213
17:13.310 --> 17:15.760
Then I will go public with the information I know.

214
17:16.600 --> 17:22.620
It'd make hiding the young lady far more difficult.

215
17:26.190 --> 17:29.160
Or do you think you can keep her hidden away forever?

216
17:30.060 --> 17:32.330
In this tiny country known as Japan?

217
17:42.100 --> 17:45.000
I propose you move to China with your daughter,

218
17:45.000 --> 17:48.160
and start a business using your cloning tech.

219
17:48.770 --> 17:51.790
I guarantee your living conditions will exponentially improve over there.

220
17:53.650 --> 17:57.000
I didn't realize Xin Ming Ah dabbled in such businesses.

221
17:58.560 --> 18:02.310
I haven't disclosed the specifics to headquarters yet.

222
18:02.310 --> 18:05.130
I am currently acting on my own accord.

223
18:07.770 --> 18:10.500
What can one man do to help us?

224
18:11.280 --> 18:13.450
Let me be your salesperson.

225
18:14.310 --> 18:18.620
The rich will buy your technology without hesitation.

226
18:19.450 --> 18:24.410
The public won't ever have to know of you and your daughter.

227
18:26.310 --> 18:28.790
You're expecting me to trust such a gamble?

228
18:30.230 --> 18:34.850
You have no other choice.

229
18:35.660 --> 18:37.450
Do you?

230
18:40.270 --> 18:45.370
I am half Chinese, half Japanese.

231
18:46.080 --> 18:48.940
In China, I'm treated as Japanese.

232
18:48.940 --> 18:52.050
In Japan, I'm treated as Chinese.

233
18:53.900 --> 18:57.200
I do not wish to be bound to one country.

234
18:58.020 --> 19:02.830
I only trust the nation known as Business.

235
19:06.350 --> 19:10.120
Please give it some thought.

236
19:11.150 --> 19:13.790
I will not give you a deadline.

237
19:18.270 --> 19:24.050
But I also cannot say when I will disclose the truth.

238
19:25.490 --> 19:30.800
Perhaps in a year. Or maybe tomorrow.

239
19:53.050 --> 19:54.490
Yes?

240
19:54.490 --> 19:57.620
Kayoko Senba is currently under our care.

241
19:57.620 --> 20:02.690
I plan to ask what happened to her.

242
20:02.690 --> 20:04.670
Is that fine by you?

243
20:04.670 --> 20:06.870
Why would I have issue with that?

244
20:06.870 --> 20:10.250
Your stepson is involved, for one.

245
20:11.230 --> 20:13.370
I see.

246
20:13.370 --> 20:16.560
When she speaks, tell me everything.

247
20:16.560 --> 20:17.910
Of course.

248
20:27.790 --> 20:30.790
Tomoe Senba was killed.

249
20:30.790 --> 20:32.600
Hey, wait.

250
20:36.120 --> 20:39.060
Everyone's connected somehow.

251
20:40.580 --> 20:43.370
If you have something, they'll come after you.

252
20:43.370 --> 20:46.840
These people are killing folks left and right

253
20:46.840 --> 20:50.960
all to keep this girl under wraps.

254
21:03.800 --> 21:05.550
Good evening.

255
21:06.500 --> 21:08.620
- You're still here? - Yeah.

256
21:08.620 --> 21:11.290
I'm organizing everything we know so far.

257
21:12.820 --> 21:16.480
This is a huge case we've got here.

258
21:17.110 --> 21:19.980
A clone? Is that true?

259
21:19.980 --> 21:25.740
I only half believe it myself. I'll try pressing Plantae about it.

260
21:25.740 --> 21:28.430
Can't wait to see how they respond.

261
21:49.830 --> 21:51.400
I'm home.

262
21:54.490 --> 21:56.250
Welcome back.

263
21:56.250 --> 21:57.720
You're always sitting there, aren't you?

264
21:57.720 --> 22:00.740
Yeah. I wait for you to come home.

265
22:00.740 --> 22:02.120
That's why?

266
22:02.120 --> 22:03.950
Yup.

267
22:03.950 --> 22:09.320
It's actually pretty nice, waiting for someone.

268
22:09.320 --> 22:11.500
You enjoy waiting?

269
22:11.500 --> 22:12.890
I do.

270
22:14.610 --> 22:19.360
If a friend kept me waiting, I'd just leave.

271
22:19.360 --> 22:26.290
I've never kept someone waiting, nor been the one waiting until now.

272
22:32.950 --> 22:34.660
It feels nice today.

273
22:34.660 --> 22:36.650
It does.

274
22:36.650 --> 22:40.170
- It's gotten warmer. - Yeah.

275
22:43.570 --> 22:48.720
Don't forget I'm waiting, okay?

276
22:51.430 --> 22:52.880
I won't.

277
22:55.490 --> 22:58.000
You'll come find me, won't you?

278
23:05.540 --> 23:07.940
Shiharu is alive.

279
23:07.940 --> 23:11.850
Shiharu is very much alive.

280
23:21.460 --> 23:23.300
[Kyoichi Nanase]

281
23:23.300 --> 23:25.570
[Mikio Maehara]

282
23:33.150 --> 23:35.790
Want to know where your sister is?

283
23:36.800 --> 23:38.250
Of course.

284
23:39.530 --> 23:41.260
I'll send you the address.

285
23:43.120 --> 23:45.420
How did you manage to find her?

286
23:47.950 --> 23:52.450
There's a building your father is renting under the name of a fake company.

287
23:52.450 --> 23:56.750
You said you wouldn't entertain my delusions.

288
23:56.750 --> 23:59.450
What changed your mind?

289
23:59.450 --> 24:02.430
I'm sure you plan to ambush me there.

290
24:03.610 --> 24:05.850
I understand why you'd think that.

291
24:08.400 --> 24:11.480
I'd make the same assumption if I were you.

292
24:11.480 --> 24:14.700
Were you ordered to trap me there?

293
24:14.700 --> 24:16.510
No.

294
24:20.490 --> 24:23.660
I can't trust your father anymore.

295
24:25.030 --> 24:27.150
What happened?

296
24:27.150 --> 24:30.160
I truly appreciate President Nanase.

297
24:30.160 --> 24:35.100
He took me in when no one else believed in me.

298
24:36.950 --> 24:39.010
I don't want to betray his generosity.

299
24:40.690 --> 24:42.420
Still...

300
24:43.580 --> 24:46.870
I also can't allow myself to sit here,

301
24:46.870 --> 24:48.620
and wait to be tossed aside.

302
24:51.330 --> 24:53.010
Alright.

303
25:03.290 --> 25:06.300
- Kasuga, your approval please. - Of course.

304
25:15.480 --> 25:17.010
Kasuga.

305
25:17.780 --> 25:20.360
The name's Tada, from the Kanzawa Station.

306
25:20.360 --> 25:22.330
I see no issues.

307
25:25.860 --> 25:29.430
Kayoko Senba is here, yes?

308
25:30.250 --> 25:36.270
I believe Dr. Senba's location was to remain a secret for her own safety?

309
25:36.270 --> 25:40.000
We must confirm something with her.

310
25:40.000 --> 25:43.290
Is this a part of an official investigation?

311
25:43.290 --> 25:46.830
I only wish to ask a few questions.

312
25:46.830 --> 25:48.580
I will pass them along,

313
25:48.580 --> 25:50.560
and contact you with her answers.

314
25:50.560 --> 25:52.970
But she is here, yes?

315
25:53.780 --> 25:58.130
I wish to speak with Kayoko Senba directly.

316
26:03.630 --> 26:05.800
Excuse me.

317
26:15.160 --> 26:17.220
Please, try to eat.

318
26:19.060 --> 26:22.940
I have business to attend to. Please leave us.

319
26:22.940 --> 26:26.080
Then I'll ask you instead.

320
26:26.770 --> 26:29.830
Your founder, Sojiro Manabe, requested Yumihiko Nanase,

321
26:29.830 --> 26:36.540
the previous Nichie head, to create a successor.

322
26:39.010 --> 26:43.430
Is that not the clone created from the remains of Roopkund?

323
26:43.430 --> 26:48.870
Or as Manabe called it, the Land of Souls?

324
26:49.980 --> 26:53.120
What are you talking about?

325
26:53.120 --> 26:57.700
Those involved in the clone research were Kayoko Senba, Kyoichi Nanase,

326
26:57.700 --> 27:01.450
and the now deceased Akihiko Ishimizaki.

327
27:01.450 --> 27:04.620
The Holy Woman they created is still alive.

328
27:04.620 --> 27:06.950
She's here, isn't she?

329
27:08.450 --> 27:10.540
A clone?

330
27:11.160 --> 27:13.570
Now that is utterly ridiculous.

331
27:13.570 --> 27:15.520
You ought to get some rest.

332
27:15.520 --> 27:17.690
Where's the Holy Woman of Plantae?

333
27:17.690 --> 27:19.850
Freeze.

334
27:21.400 --> 27:23.160
What's up, Mayuzumi?

335
27:23.160 --> 27:26.350
Was she filed with an arrest warrant?

336
27:28.370 --> 27:30.480
You are under arrest

337
27:30.480 --> 27:33.800
for harboring a fugitive, and sharing classified intel.

338
27:34.760 --> 27:38.450
Tada.

339
27:38.450 --> 27:40.840
What the...

340
27:40.840 --> 27:43.100
What's going on? Hey!

341
27:43.100 --> 27:46.120
Mayuzumi! Let me go!

342
27:48.610 --> 27:50.180
You...

343
27:50.180 --> 27:51.420
Come on.

344
27:51.420 --> 27:54.080
- Let me go! - Walk!

345
27:54.080 --> 27:56.600
Mayuzumi, what's going on? Mayuzumi!

346
27:56.600 --> 27:58.850
- I said, walk! - Hey!

347
27:58.850 --> 28:00.720
Let me go, damn it! Mayuzumi!

348
28:00.720 --> 28:02.940
Keep moving!

349
28:02.940 --> 28:07.780
He said the Holy Woman created from the Roopkund remains

350
28:07.780 --> 28:10.620
is still alive.

351
28:12.540 --> 28:15.420
It's possible she is.

352
28:26.630 --> 28:30.250
No! I was set up!

353
28:30.250 --> 28:32.730
Sounds like quite the ruckus.

354
28:33.560 --> 28:36.390
It's probably my fault.

355
28:37.030 --> 28:39.490
I'll go see what's going on.

356
28:39.490 --> 28:41.800
Don't leave me alone!

357
28:44.240 --> 28:45.950
Please...

358
28:50.020 --> 28:51.810
Alright.

359
28:52.410 --> 28:54.340
Let's go together.

360
28:58.570 --> 29:02.390
Hey! Let me go, damn it!

361
29:07.410 --> 29:10.740
You bastards are falling for it!

362
29:10.740 --> 29:12.400
Are you listening?

363
29:12.400 --> 29:14.430
- Let's return to your room. - Hey!

364
29:18.480 --> 29:22.720
I was set up! It's all a trick!

365
29:48.690 --> 29:50.260
Hello?

366
30:00.160 --> 30:03.220
I appreciate the swift response.

367
30:07.370 --> 30:09.690
I grew tired of overthinking things.

368
30:09.690 --> 30:16.390
I would first like to see the potential of your "human cloning" technology.

369
30:16.960 --> 30:19.480
I suppose you do.

370
30:19.480 --> 30:22.010
May I meet the young lady?

371
30:25.310 --> 30:28.080
She is currently being harbored at a certain facility.

372
30:28.700 --> 30:31.920
One I'd prefer to keep a secret from others.

373
30:31.920 --> 30:34.540
I understand entirely.

374
30:37.740 --> 30:41.900
This is your key in. I'll send the address later.

375
30:41.900 --> 30:44.020
I will meet you there.

376
30:44.790 --> 30:46.430
Excellent.

377
31:08.850 --> 31:10.680
Mayuzumi.

378
31:11.780 --> 31:13.990
I'm sorry I couldn't come the other day.

379
31:13.990 --> 31:16.990
- It's fine. - Things became quite hectic for us.

380
31:16.990 --> 31:20.930
Does it have anything to do with Haruka Nanase?

381
31:21.620 --> 31:24.640
We think so, but we're not certain yet.

382
31:26.730 --> 31:29.390
You know Kayoko Senba, right?

383
31:29.390 --> 31:30.600
Huh?

384
31:30.600 --> 31:33.950
You were seen on her intercom.

385
31:37.520 --> 31:40.250
Oh, at the time, I...

386
31:41.100 --> 31:43.110
Relax.

387
31:43.110 --> 31:48.810
I'm not asking you as an officer. I'm just trying to help find Shiharu.

388
31:49.320 --> 31:50.800
Right.

389
31:51.660 --> 31:55.740
Dr. Senba is currently with an acquaintance of mine.

390
31:55.740 --> 31:58.230
Will you come with me to speak to her?

391
32:01.610 --> 32:04.690
You don't have to talk about anything you don't want to.

392
32:04.690 --> 32:09.120
I just thought Dr. Senba may open up to you.

393
32:09.120 --> 32:13.770
Did something happen to Dr. Senba?

394
32:13.770 --> 32:14.690
Why ask?

395
32:14.690 --> 32:19.890
Well, I wondered why she was with an acquaintance at all.

396
32:22.150 --> 32:24.980
I'll tell you more once we're there.

397
32:26.060 --> 32:30.330
Dr. Senba knew your father as well, right?

398
32:31.480 --> 32:33.400
Yes.

399
32:33.400 --> 32:36.430
Do you think she knows about Shiharu?

400
32:38.900 --> 32:40.680
Probably.

401
32:41.440 --> 32:43.390
Then let's go see her.

402
32:48.060 --> 32:51.770
Where exactly are we going?

403
32:51.770 --> 32:55.650
A place where my acquaintances often gather.

404
32:55.650 --> 32:58.580
Dr. Senba feels at ease there as well.

405
33:00.490 --> 33:02.560
No need to be so nervous.

406
33:02.560 --> 33:05.890
What I want to talk about is unrelated to police business.

407
33:05.890 --> 33:08.530
Is that allowed?

408
33:12.190 --> 33:13.790
Be right back.

409
33:18.230 --> 33:19.940
Hello?

410
33:19.940 --> 33:24.030
I'm sorry. Kayoko Senba got away.

411
33:24.030 --> 33:26.000
What happened?

412
33:27.910 --> 33:30.920
Everyone's only focused on their own selfish goals.

413
33:32.790 --> 33:35.080
No one actually cares about whether you,

414
33:36.520 --> 33:39.160
or Shiharu are safe.

415
33:41.410 --> 33:45.900
We're searching the perimeters for her, but I think she's long gone.

416
33:45.900 --> 33:47.770
I see.

417
33:47.770 --> 33:51.030
I was about to bring Mari Ishimizaki over...

418
33:51.030 --> 33:52.190
Bring her anyway.

419
33:52.190 --> 33:55.390
I have many things to ask her.

420
33:55.980 --> 33:57.630
Understood.

421
34:26.840 --> 34:30.590
It's highly likely your sister is being kept here.

422
34:37.360 --> 34:39.370
Everything is going as planned.

423
34:39.370 --> 34:41.610
I'll get my hands on it soon.

424
36:57.270 --> 36:59.150
Mr. Nanase?

425
37:08.800 --> 37:11.370
Ah, you must be one of the staff.

426
37:12.220 --> 37:15.250
I came at Mr. Nanase's request.

427
37:17.670 --> 37:22.510
Where is the individual who was in this bed?

428
40:24.020 --> 40:25.990
Where are you?

429
40:25.990 --> 40:29.400
Some lab Maehara told me about. He said Shiharu would be here.

430
40:29.400 --> 40:32.270
Maehara... So was she there?

431
40:32.270 --> 40:35.690
No. I found Xin Ming Ah's Kojima, dead.

432
40:35.690 --> 40:37.000
Damn.

433
40:37.000 --> 40:39.440
Kyoichi Nanase arrived soon after.

434
40:39.440 --> 40:42.390
I think he came to see if Kojima was dead.

435
40:42.940 --> 40:45.300
Then Kyoichi Nanase ordered the hit on him?

436
40:45.880 --> 40:47.660
I'll ask him.

437
40:47.660 --> 40:49.800
What?

438
40:51.620 --> 40:54.050
I'll finish this myself.

439
40:55.540 --> 40:57.980
Tada was arrested.

440
40:59.490 --> 41:02.310
Something's odd about his arrest.

441
41:02.310 --> 41:05.580
I can only imagine it's their doing.

442
41:05.580 --> 41:09.130
We know too much. Who knows what'll happen to us?

443
41:10.290 --> 41:12.740
We don't stand a chance against them.

444
41:13.410 --> 41:15.700
Back off while you can.

445
41:15.700 --> 41:17.160
I refuse.

446
41:17.160 --> 41:21.190
They've infiltrated the police. My workplace isn't safe either.

447
41:21.190 --> 41:22.940
If you keep pressing,

448
41:22.940 --> 41:27.300
they'll melt you, or arrest you for some bogus crime.

449
41:28.690 --> 41:30.540
I'm going to go see Kyoichi Nanase.

450
41:30.540 --> 41:33.370
See him, and then what?

451
41:33.370 --> 41:36.080
I need to know the truth.

452
41:36.080 --> 41:38.220
Don't do it!

453
41:41.150 --> 41:43.420
I'll end things here.

454
41:44.530 --> 41:47.040
If you eventually can't reach me,

455
41:47.040 --> 41:51.160
publish everything in an article, on social media. Wherever.

456
41:51.160 --> 41:53.300
Everything? But you'll...

457
41:54.940 --> 41:56.850
I don't care what happens to me.

458
41:58.400 --> 42:00.210
I don't care if I die.

459
42:02.860 --> 42:04.750
I just...

460
42:06.620 --> 42:08.910
I want to see Shiharu, one last time.

461
42:24.170 --> 42:26.000
Mayuzumi.

462
42:27.330 --> 42:31.210
You were with Plantae all along.

463
42:31.980 --> 42:33.980
Come on.

464
42:33.980 --> 42:36.560
You're working for them, aren't you?

465
42:36.560 --> 42:40.120
You're no cop. You're just a lackey!

466
42:40.120 --> 42:42.170
Move it!

467
42:49.940 --> 42:52.650
Sorry, cancel all my plans today.

468
42:52.650 --> 42:54.070
Everything, sir?

469
42:54.070 --> 42:56.000
Yes, everything.

470
42:56.000 --> 42:58.010
Understood.

471
43:12.450 --> 43:14.320
You called?

472
43:14.320 --> 43:16.020
Yes.

473
43:16.020 --> 43:18.500
I wanted to talk in person. Alone.

474
43:18.500 --> 43:21.880
I'm glad you're ready. Let's agree on where to meet.

475
43:21.880 --> 43:23.780
Alright.

476
43:23.780 --> 43:26.420
Will you come to Yamashiro Art Gallery?

477
43:29.960 --> 43:32.040
That's where Shiharu is.

478
43:36.360 --> 43:41.000
I'll join you once I finish one last errand.

479
43:41.580 --> 43:43.200
Wait for me there.

480
44:28.690 --> 44:31.580
I can't trust a word that man says.

481
44:32.380 --> 44:38.450
But no one else knows where Shiharu is.
